---
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";
import ContactLine from "../components/ContactLine.astro";
import { PAGES } from "../lib/pages";
import { OPERATOR } from "../lib/site";
import { PLANS, trialDays, GUARANTEE, RETENTION_DAYS as R } from "../lib/app";
const page = PAGES.terms;
---

<Doc page={page} heading="Terms of service" intro="The terms for using the CRO Toolbox Shopify app and this website." updated="October 19, 2026">
  <p>
    These terms are an agreement between you (the merchant installing the app) and {OPERATOR} ("we"), who runs CRO Toolbox. By installing or using
    the app you accept them. Shopify's own terms also apply to your use of Shopify.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    CRO Toolbox is a Shopify app that adds offers, bundles, storefront sections and widgets, cart offers, checkout rules and analytics to your store.
    We may improve, change or remove features over time.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Plans, trials and billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The {PLANS.free.name} plan is free. Paid plans are billed by Shopify, monthly or yearly, at the prices shown on our pricing page and in the app.</li>
    <li>Paid plans start with a {trialDays} day free trial. If you cancel during the trial, you are not charged.</li>
    <li>{GUARANTEE} Charges already billed by Shopify are not refunded, except where the law requires it.</li>
    <li>Plans include monthly order limits. They are soft: if your store goes over, the app reminds you to move up a plan and nothing is switched off.</li>
    <li>We may change prices with at least 30 days' notice in the app. Your current billing period is not affected.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You are responsible for the offers, prices, discounts, texts, images and reviews you publish with the app, and for checking them before they go live.</li>
    <li>You are responsible for following the laws that apply to your store, including consumer, pricing and privacy laws, and for your own privacy policy towards your shoppers.</li>
    <li>Use countdown timers, stock messages and similar features honestly. Don't show false urgency or fake reviews.</li>
    <li>Don't misuse the app: no attempts to break, overload, copy or resell it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Your data and data processing</h2>
  <p>
    Your store's data stays yours. We use it only to run the app, as described in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. Most app settings are
    saved in your own store.
  </p>
  <p>For personal data of your customers and visitors that the app processes for you, you are the controller and we are your processor. We:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>process it only to provide the app's features to your store, and never sell it or use it for advertising;</li>
    <li>keep only the minimum the features need, delete it after the periods in our privacy policy, and delete all of it when you uninstall;</li>
    <li>use only the service providers listed in our privacy policy, under the same obligations;</li>
    <li>protect it with encryption in transit and at rest, encrypted backups and access limited to the people who run the app;</li>
    <li>handle your customers' access and deletion requests that Shopify sends us, and help you answer them;</li>
    <li>respect your customers' consent choices made in your store's cookie banner;</li>
    <li>tell Shopify and you within 72 hours if a security incident affects personal data we hold for your store.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the app running and fix problems quickly, but the app is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. Parts of the app run on
    Shopify, so Shopify outages and changes can affect it.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost sales or profits. Our total liability is limited
    to the fees you paid us in the 12 months before the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Ending</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop at any time by uninstalling the app. We may suspend or end access if these terms are seriously broken. After uninstalling, your data
    is deleted as our privacy policy describes.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. For important changes we tell you in the app at least 30 days before they apply.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <ContactLine />.</p>
</Doc>
